course: dictionary
lesson: 1231
title: Bullfighter
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A bullfighter is a person who takes part in a bullfight. A bullfight is a public show in which people tease and fight a bull, and it usually ends with the bull being killed. The main bullfighter is called a matador.
explain: Bullfighting is a tradition in Spain, Portugal, southern France and parts of Latin America. Many people think it is cruel to animals, and some places have banned it. Culture lessons ask you to think about both sides and explain why people disagree.
explain: In stories, a bullfighter waves a red cape. «Cattle cannot see red the way we do, and a bull charges a matador's cape (the cloth a bullfighter waves) because it moves, not because it is red.» So the bull reacts to movement, not colour.
fact: A bullfighter takes part in a bullfight, a public show in which people tease and fight a bull.
fact: The main bullfighter is called a matador.
fact: Myth: bulls are not angered by the colour red; they react to the cape moving.
fact: «Bulls see red poorly and charge at a matador's cape (the cloth a bullfighter waves) because it moves, whatever its colour.»
fact: Bullfighting is a tradition in Spain, Portugal, southern France and parts of Latin America, but some places have banned it.
exercise: The main bullfighter is called what? | A bull | A stadium | A cape | *A matador
exercise: Why does a bull charge a matador's cape? | It wants to eat the cloth | It is hungry | It is angry at the colour red | *It reacts to the cape moving
exercise: What is a bullfight? | A race between horses | *A public show in which people tease and fight a bull | A school sports day | A quiet walk through a farm
test: Which country is named in the lessons as a place where bullfighting is a tradition? | *Spain | Canada | Norway | Japan
test: Many people think bullfighting is what? | A cheap sport for children | *Cruel to animals | Good for bulls | A kind of dance
exam: According to the myth in the lessons, what makes a bull charge? | The noise of the crowd | *The cape moving | The colour red alone | Hunger
